ARTICLE 1 — DEFINITIONS
===============================================================================

1.1 "Software" means the Kevrai Omni computer program, including its source
    code, object code, documentation, configuration files, build scripts,
    catalog data (including the model and engine metadata in the `catalog/`
    directory), graphical assets, user interface designs, logos (subject to
    Article 13), the local agent subsystem, application programming
    interfaces (APIs), and any other materials distributed with or as part of
    Kevrai Omni, in each case as made available by the Licensor, in any
    version and in any medium.

    For the avoidance of doubt, "Software" does NOT include any third-party
    model weights, engine binaries, datasets, or other components listed in
    the `catalog/` directory or downloaded on demand by the Software. Each
    such third-party component is governed by its own upstream license, as
    documented in the `NOTICE.md` file accompanying the Software.

1.2 "Derivative Works" means any work, whether in source or object form, that
    is based upon, derived from, or incorporates the Software or any portion
    thereof, including but not limited to: modifications, translations,
    adaptations, annotations, compilations, patches, plugins, extensions,
    forks, ports, packaged distributions, container images, and any larger
    work in which the Software or its Derivative Works are embedded or with
    which they are combined. The boundary between a Derivative Work and a
    separate independent work is explained in Section 4.8 and Appendix E.

1.3 "Distribution" means any act of making the Software or its Derivative
    Works available to any third party, including but not limited to:
    (a) providing copies for download;
    (b) pre-installing the Software on hardware;
    (c) offering the Software as a hosted, software-as-a-service (SaaS),
        platform-as-a-service (PaaS), infrastructure-as-a-service (IaaS), or
        any other remotely accessible service (see also "Network Use" in
        Section 1.12);
    (d) distributing the Software as part of a commercial product or bundle;
    (e) distributing the Software through an application store, software
        marketplace, package registry, or any digital distribution channel;
    (f) making the Source Code available via a public version control
        repository, code hosting platform, or mirror;
    (g) timesharing, service bureau, or managed-service arrangements in which
        a third party interacts with the Software operated by you.

1.4 "Commercial Use" means any use of the Software or its Derivative Works
    that is primarily intended for or directed toward commercial advantage or
    monetary compensation, including but not limited to:
    (a) selling, licensing, leasing, renting, or sublicensing the Software or
        its Derivative Works for a fee or other consideration (including
        in-kind consideration and advertising revenue);
    (b) using the Software or its Derivative Works in the production
        environment of any business, enterprise, institution, organization,
        or government body to support its principal business operations or to
        provide products or services to external customers;
    (c) using the Software or its Derivative Works to provide paid services,
        consulting, custom development, technical support, hosting, or
        training to third parties;
    (d) distributing the Software or its Derivative Works through an
        application store, software marketplace, or any platform where revenue
        or traffic share is generated;
    (e) using the Software or its Derivative Works to generate content, data,
        or outputs that are sold, licensed, or otherwise monetized, where the
        Software is a material component of the value proposition;
    (f) using the Software or its Derivative Works by or on behalf of any
        entity with more than ten (10) employees or more than USD 1,000,000 in
        annual revenue (on a consolidated basis with Affiliates), unless such
        use is solely for internal evaluation, testing, or prototyping that
        does not support revenue-generating operations and that complies with
        Section 1.4(iv);
    (g) using the Software or its Derivative Works to develop, operate, or
        distribute any Competing Product;
    (h) any timesharing, rental, leasing, service bureau, managed-service, or
        outsourcing arrangement in which third parties obtain the functional
        benefit of the Software, whether or not a separate fee is charged
        specifically for the Software.

    The following do NOT constitute Commercial Use, provided they do not
    otherwise fall within the foregoing categories:
    (i) personal learning, experimentation, or hobbyist use by an individual;
    (ii) academic research, teaching, or educational demonstration by an
         accredited educational institution or an individual student or
         researcher, where the results are published openly;
    (iii) technical evaluation, benchmarking, interoperability research, or
         review;
    (iv) internal non-commercial trial or prototyping within an organization
         that is not used to support revenue-generating operations or external
         customer-facing products or services, and that does not exceed ninety
         (90) consecutive days in duration and ten (10) named users;
    (v) contributing bug fixes, documentation improvements, or code
         contributions back to the Software's official repository;
    (vi) use by a registered non-profit, charity, or non-governmental
         organization whose activities are not directed toward commercial
         advantage, subject to prior written confirmation by the Licensor on
         request.

1.5 "Licensor" means the copyright holder of the Software, namely Kevrai
    Omni contributors, and any successor in interest or assignee under
    Section 19.11.

1.6 "Commercial Authorization" means a written authorization issued by the
    Licensor to a specific licensee, granting permission to use the Software
    or its Derivative Works for specified Commercial Use purposes. A
    Commercial Authorization may be in the form of a signed paper document,
    an electronically signed document (including via valid electronic
    signature platforms), or a written confirmation issued through the
    Licensor's official contact channels (including the email address listed
    in Appendix A). A Commercial Authorization is personal to the named
    licensee and may not be assigned or transferred except as expressly
    permitted by Section 5.5.

1.7 "Notice File" means the `NOTICE.md` file distributed with the Software,
    which contains attribution information, third-party component license
    notices, and other required notices.

1.8 "Modification" means any alteration, addition, deletion, or other change
    to the Software, whether in source code, object code, documentation,
    catalog data, or any other form. A "Modified Version" means the Software
    as changed by one or more Modifications. A "Fork" means a Modified Version
    maintained in a separate source repository or distribution channel.

1.9 "Affiliate" means, with respect to any entity, any other entity that
    directly or indirectly controls, is controlled by, or is under common
    control with such entity, where "control" means the ownership of more than
    fifty percent (50%) of the voting securities or the power to direct the
    management and policies of such entity. For the avoidance of doubt, a
    Commercial Authorization issued to one entity does not extend to its
    Affiliates unless expressly stated in the Commercial Authorization. For
    the purposes of the employee and revenue thresholds in Section 1.4(f), the
    employees and revenues of all Affiliates shall be aggregated on a
    consolidated basis.

1.10 "Effective Date" means the date on which you first access, install,
     copy, or use the Software, whichever occurs first.

1.11 "Source Code" means the preferred form of the Software for making
     modifications, including all source code files, build scripts,
     configuration files, catalog data, documentation, interface
     definitions, and any other files necessary to compile, build, install,
     and run the Software. "Effective Source Code" means Source Code that is:
     (a) complete, including every component required to generate, install,
         and run the corresponding object code or service, together with
         build and installation instructions and any control scripts;
     (b) in a human-readable, non-obfuscated, non-minified form suitable for
         modification by a reasonably skilled developer;
     (c) genuinely and reliably accessible to the general public without
         payment, login, access request, or other barrier (other than
         ordinary network access);
     (d) available in a commonly used, machine-readable format.
     Obfuscated code, disassembly output, stub files, or source code from
     which material components have been omitted does not constitute
     Effective Source Code.

1.12 "Network Use" means any use of the Software or its Derivative Works in
     which the Software is made available to, or accessed by, users over a
     computer network (including the internet, an intranet, a virtual private
     network, or any other network), whether or not such use is for
     Commercial Use. Network Use includes, without limitation, offering the
     Software as a SaaS, PaaS, or IaaS service, providing access to the
     Software via an API, web interface, or remote procedure call, and
     embedding the Software in a network-accessible application or service.
     For the avoidance of doubt, Network Use constitutes Distribution for
     purposes of this License.

1.13 "User Data" means any data, content, or information that is input into,
     processed by, generated by, or stored through the Software or its
     Derivative Works by or on behalf of you or your End Users, including but
     not limited to personal data, sensitive personal data, model inputs and
     Outputs, configuration data, telemetry, and usage data.

1.14 "Security Incident" means any actual or reasonably suspected
     unauthorized access, use, disclosure, alteration, or destruction of the
     Software, User Data, or any system on which the Software is deployed,
     including but not limited to data breaches, malware infections,
     unauthorized privilege escalation, supply-chain compromise, and
     denial-of-service attacks that materially affect the availability or
     integrity of the Software.

1.15 "Prohibited Use" means any use of the Software or its Derivative Works
     that is prohibited under Article 7 (Responsible AI Use and Prohibited
     Uses), Article 17 (Anti-Evasion), Article 18 (AI Training and
     Competitive Restrictions), or Appendix C (Prohibited Uses List).

1.16 "Third-Party Component" means any software, model weight, dataset,
     engine binary, library, framework, or other component that is not part
     of the Software but is referenced by, downloaded by, or used in
     conjunction with the Software, including but not limited to the items
     listed in the `catalog/` directory and the `NOTICE.md` file.

1.17 "Contribution" means any work of authorship, including source code,
     documentation, bug fixes, feature additions, catalog entries, or other
     modifications, that is submitted by you to the Licensor for inclusion in
     the Software, whether via a pull request, patch, merge request, issue
     comment, email, or any other submission mechanism.

1.18 "End User" means any natural person or legal entity that accesses or
     uses the Software, a Derivative Work, or any service powered thereby,
     other than you.

1.19 "Arms-Length Interface" means a well-documented, stable interface using
     standard, generic data formats and protocols (such as HTTP/REST with
     JSON, command-line invocation with plain-text or standard-format
     arguments and outputs, or an open standardized protocol), through which
     two programs exchange data without sharing internal data structures,
     memory address space, or proprietary programmatic interfaces, and
     without one program being specifically designed to depend on the
     internal implementation details of the other.

1.20 "Model" means any machine learning or artificial intelligence model,
     including its weights, parameters, tokenizer, configuration, and
     associated inference logic, that is managed, downloaded, invoked, or
     operated by or through the Software.

1.21 "Output" means any content, data, result, or response generated by a
     Model when invoked through the Software.

1.22 "Distillation" means the process of deriving a new model, system, or
     dataset from the Software, a Model, or Outputs, including by using
     Outputs as training or evaluation data, extracting behavioral
     signatures, compressing or transferring capabilities, or replicating
     functionality, whether by machine learning, statistical analysis, manual
     transcription, or any other method.

1.23 "Competing Product" means any product, service, model, system, or
     offering that substitutes for, or is functionally substantially similar
     to, the Software or any material feature thereof, including a local AI
     model manager, a local AI workstation/orchestrator, or a bundled local
     inference and model-management platform.

1.24 "Personal Data" and "Sensitive Personal Data" have the meanings given
     to them under applicable data protection law (including, where
     applicable, the Personal Information Protection Law of the PRC and the
     GDPR).

