ARTICLE 5 — COMMERCIAL USE AUTHORIZATION
===============================================================================

5.1 Commercial Use Requires Prior Written Authorization. Notwithstanding any
    other provision of this License, you may NOT use the Software or any
    Derivative Work for any Commercial Use unless and until you have obtained
    a valid, written Commercial Authorization from the Licensor that
    specifically covers such Commercial Use. Any Commercial Use undertaken
    without a valid Commercial Authorization constitutes a material breach of
    this License and an infringement of the Licensor's intellectual property
    rights, for which the Licensor may elect remedies in contract, tort, or
    under intellectual-property statutes.

5.2 Application Process. To apply for a Commercial Authorization, you must
    submit a written application to the Licensor at the contact address
    specified in Appendix A. Your application must include, at a minimum:
    (a) the legal name, registration number (e.g., unified social credit code
        or equivalent), principal place of business, and contact information
        of the applicant;
    (b) the names and contact information of any Affiliates that will use the
        Software under the Commercial Authorization, if applicable, and
        consolidated employee count and annual revenue;
    (c) the specific version(s) of the Software you intend to use;
    (d) a detailed description of the intended Commercial Use, including
        whether it involves internal use, redistribution, SaaS/PaaS hosting,
        embedding in hardware, timesharing/service-bureau arrangements, or any
        other form;
    (e) the intended business scenario, target market, and estimated user
        scale and deployment scale;
    (f) whether you intend to distribute any Derivative Work in closed-source
        or proprietary form, and if so, the proposed distribution model;
    (g) a description of the data types and volumes expected to be processed
        through the Software, including whether any Personal Data or Sensitive
        Personal Data will be processed, and any cross-border transfers;
    (h) a description of the security measures you have implemented or will
        implement to protect the Software and User Data;
    (i) whether you intend to train, fine-tune, distill, or otherwise use the
        Software or Outputs in connection with any other model or Competing
        Product (see Article 18);
    (j) evidence of the insurance coverage required by Section 5.10, if
        applicable;
    (k) any other information reasonably requested by the Licensor.

    A template for the Commercial Authorization application is provided in
    Appendix B.

5.3 Evaluation and Grant. The Licensor shall use reasonable endeavors to
    respond to a complete application within thirty (30) business days of
