     (a) preliminary and permanent injunctive relief and specific performance;
     (b) behavior-preservation / act-omission preservation orders (行为保全)
         requiring you to cease or refrain from specified conduct;
     (c) evidence-preservation orders (证据保全) to secure evidence of
         infringement;
     (d) property-preservation orders (财产保全) to secure eventual judgment;
     in any court or tribunal of competent jurisdiction, without the
     requirement to post a bond or prove actual damages to the extent
     permitted by law.

12.3 Damages and Account of Profits. In the event of any breach of this
     License, the Licensor shall be entitled to elect and recover from the
     breaching party, on the basis most favorable to the Licensor permitted by
     applicable law:
     (a) all actual damages suffered by the Licensor as a result of the breach;
     (b) an account of all profits, revenues, or other benefits derived by the
         breaching party from the unauthorized use, distribution, or
         exploitation of the Software or any Derivative Work;
     (c) reasonable royalty / licensing fees that would have been payable for
         lawful use;
     (d) statutory damages (法定赔偿) where available under applicable law
         (including, under PRC law as in force from time to time, statutory
         copyright damages within the statutory cap);
     (e) punitive or exemplary damages (惩罚性赔偿) for willful, malicious, or
         repeated infringement, in the multiples permitted by applicable law;
     (f) liquidated damages for unauthorized Commercial Use, in an amount equal
         to the greatest of: (i) the reasonable licensing fees that the
         Licensor would have charged for the unauthorized Commercial Use;
         (ii) USD 10,000 per instance of unauthorized Commercial Use (with
         each distinct deployment, product, service, customer, or continuous
         thirty-day period of unauthorized use counting as a separate
         instance); or (iii) the actual damages suffered by the Licensor. The
         parties agree that this liquidated damages provision is a reasonable
         estimate of the Licensor's probable loss in the event of unauthorized
         Commercial Use and is not a penalty; if a competent authority
         considers the amount excessive, it shall be reduced only to the
         highest amount that such authority considers enforceable.

12.4 Limited Cure Period. In the case of a non-commercial, unintentional, and
     non-willful breach of this License (excluding any unauthorized Commercial
