ARTICLE 16 — TERMINATION
===============================================================================

16.1 Automatic Termination for Breach. If you breach any term or condition of
     this License, all rights and licenses granted to you under this License
     (including the copyright license under Article 2 and the patent license
     under Article 3) shall terminate automatically and immediately, without
     the need for any notice from the Licensor, unless the breach is a
     non-commercial, unintentional, and curable breach as described in
     Section 12.4 and is cured within the applicable cure period.

16.2 Effect of Termination. Upon termination of this License for any reason:
     (a) you must immediately cease all use, reproduction, modification, and
         distribution of the Software and all Derivative Works, and must cease
         any Network Use;
     (b) you must destroy or permanently delete all copies of the Software and
         all Derivative Works in your possession, custody, or control
         (including production, backup, and cloud environments, subject to
         legally required retention), and certify such destruction in writing
         upon request by the Licensor;
     (c) any sublicenses previously granted by you to third parties shall
         terminate, except that copies lawfully distributed to third parties
         prior to termination may continue to be used by such third parties
         solely to the extent such third parties remain in compliance with this
         License;
     (d) any Commercial Authorization held by you shall terminate immediately,
         unless the Commercial Authorization expressly provides for survival
         upon termination of this License;
     (e) you must immediately pay the Licensor all fees and amounts accrued
         and unpaid as of the termination date.

16.3 Survival. The following provisions shall survive termination of this
     License: Article 1 (Definitions), Article 6 (Data Privacy and Security),
     Article 7 (Responsible AI Use), Article 8 (Export Control), Article 9
     (Contributions), Article 11 (Indemnification), Article 12 (Enforcement
     and Remedies), Article 13 (Trademarks), Article 14 (Disclaimer of
     Warranty), Article 15 (Limitation of Liability), Article 16
     (Termination), Article 17 (Anti-Evasion), Article 18 (AI Training and
     Competitive Restrictions), and Article 19 (General Provisions), together
     with any other provisions that by their nature are intended to survive
     termination.

16.4 No Waiver by Termination. Termination of this License shall not affect
     any right or remedy of the Licensor that has accrued prior to or as a
     result of such termination, including the right to seek damages,
     injunctive relief, or any other remedy for any breach that occurred prior
     to termination.

16.5 Termination for Convenience by Licensor. The Licensor may terminate this
     License at any time, for any reason or no reason, by providing thirty
     (30) days' prior written notice to you. Upon such termination, you must
     comply with the obligations set forth in Section 16.2. For the avoidance
     of doubt, termination for convenience by the Licensor does not affect any
     rights or remedies that have accrued prior to the effective date of
     termination, and the Licensor shall refund any prepaid, unused fees under
     a Commercial Authorization on a pro-rata basis.

16.6 Reinstatement. Where a breach is curable under Section 12.4 and is cured
     within the cure period, your licenses are automatically reinstated
     retroactively, provided that reinstatement does not affect the Licensor's
     rights for the period of breach.

