ARTICLE 18 — AI TRAINING, DISTILLATION, AND COMPETITIVE RESTRICTIONS
===============================================================================

18.1 Restriction on Training and Distillation. Except as expressly authorized
     by a valid Commercial Authorization or by a separate written agreement
     with the Licensor, you may not use the Software, any Model accessed
     through the Software, any Outputs, or any catalog or metadata of the
     Software, to:
     (a) train, pre-train, fine-tune, instruction-tune, align, calibrate,
         evaluate for the purpose of replicating, or otherwise improve or
         create any AI model or system that is, or is intended to become, a
         Competing Product, or whose capabilities are derived from the
         Software or such Models;
     (b) Distill the Software, any Model, or any Outputs into another model,
         dataset, system, or product, including by using Outputs as
         training, validation, or evaluation data, or by extracting
         behavioral signatures, prompts, system instructions, agent tool
         definitions, or workflows;
     (c) scrape, crawl, harvest, extract, or bulk-download the Software's
         catalog, metadata, agent prompts, tool definitions, or APIs to build
         or improve any database, model, or Competing Product;
     (d) reverse-engineer, extract, reconstruct, or replicate the weights,
         parameters, or internal representations of any Model accessed through
         the Software, except to the extent the Model's own upstream license
         expressly permits such activity;
     (e) benchmark the Software or Models for the purpose of developing or
         marketing a Competing Product (benchmarking for non-commercial
         evaluation under Section 1.4(iii) remains permitted, subject to
         Section 18.3);
     (f) use the Software or Outputs to provide a service that substitutes
         for the Software or that enables third parties to obtain the
         functional benefit of the Software without a Commercial
         Authorization.

18.2 Non-Commercial Research Exception. Nothing in Section 18.1 prohibits
     bona fide, non-commercial academic or independent research that is
     published openly and that is not used, directly or indirectly, to develop
     or improve a Competing Product or any commercial product or service.

18.3 Benchmarking. You may publish independent benchmarks and comparative
     evaluations of the Software, provided that: (a) they are truthful,
     accurate, and not misleading; (b) they disclose methodology, versions,
     and dates; (c) they do not disclose confidential information; and (d) they
     do not serve as a substitute for the Software or facilitate a Competing
     Product.

18.4 Outputs and Downstream Models. Any model, dataset, or system created in
     violation of this Article 18 is itself subject to the restrictions of
     this License to the extent it is derived from the Software, and its
     distribution or Network Use constitutes a breach.

18.5 Interaction with Upstream Model Licenses. This Article 18 supplements,
     and does not replace, the restrictions in the upstream licenses of
     Models; the more restrictive of this Article 18 and the applicable
     upstream license governs.

